Hi,

Is there a way of becoming _visible_ again? 

Yesterday I zapped myself with a wand of make invisible. 
I don't normally do this, but due to a series of bad decisions, my
armor had desintegrated, I had a cursed bow welded to my hands
and there were quite a few nasties around (I was in level 12 or
so.)  I decided that discretion would be the smartest move under
the circurstances...

It did work, I made it back up to level one where I knew there
was an altar, coverted it, sacrficed a lot (all the time
``bashing monsters my bow'' and kicking) and when I finally
prayed Crom was happy enough to uncurse my bow (and a cursed
helm as well, it was one of those days when you try everything
you find :)

Needless to say, I wouldn't have managed any of this were I not
strong as a bull.  This cannot be stressed enough: if you're a
newbie like me and want a chance of lasting more than fifteen
minutes, play a tough character like a barbarian or samurai.
With any luck your barbarian has something like 80 hit points by
the end of level four or so, so you stand a chance of surviving
an encounter with something more dangerous than a grid bug.
When I play an elf I never get anywhere :-(

Anyway, the permanent invisibility then became a problem because
shopkeepers wouldn't let me into their shops.  I had to resort
to killing them, and I'm not sure whether or not Crom
appreciates this.  For a neutral character, however, I can argue
thi both ways.  Besides, they are a bit dangerous for a
character at the level I was.  That wand of lightining and the
ring of regeneration did come in handy once or twice.

Anyways, I was piping along quite well, but then got killed
instantly by an energy vortex :( 
I had never met one, so I assumed they were mostly harmless, 
as dust vortices are.  Not so :)

The invisibility was just an inconvenience that I'd have liked to get
rid if possible.  Otherwise, killing the shopkeepers has it
funny side too, so it's not too bad.

Come to think of it, would a wand of cancellation have worked?

Bye bye, and a blessed luckstone to all.
